course: dictionary
lesson: 6773
title: Opposite: different, facing, or across
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word opposite can work in more than one way, and the sentence tells you which way. First, opposite means as different as can be: «up is the opposite of down». Second, it means facing, on the other side: «the shop opposite the school» is across the road from it. Third, in shapes, opposite sides or angles sit across from each other.
explain: Look at the little clues around the word. In «To find how many there were at the start, begin at the end and undo each step in the opposite order», opposite means reverse, so you go backwards. The word is used as an adjective here, describing the order. Opposite can also be a noun, as in «the opposite of hot is cold».
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «The shop is opposite the school», try "the shop is on the other side from the school". It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Opposite means as different as can be, like hot and cold, or up and down.
fact: Opposite can also mean facing, on the other side, as in «the shop opposite the school».
fact: In maths, opposite sides of a rectangle are equal in length.
fact: The opposite of a number like 5 is −5, and in science, opposite poles of magnets attract.
fact: Some words mean their own opposite: «dust» can mean take dust off or put powder on.
exercise: To find how many there were at the start, you undo each step in the opposite order. What does opposite order mean here? | The same order as before | Alphabetical order | *The reverse order, going backwards | Random order
exercise: Up is the opposite of which word? | over | around | sideways | *down
exercise: «The shop is opposite the school.» What does opposite mean here? | *On the other side, facing it | The same as it | Underneath it | Very different from it
test: «Across the road there may be a counter-protest with the opposite view, and both sides are allowed to protest peacefully.» What does the opposite view mean? | *A view that is different from the first one | A view hidden behind a tree | A better view | The same view as the first one
test: «Colours opposite each other on the wheel, like orange and blue, make each other shout.» Which pair sits opposite each other on the colour wheel? | Black and white | Blue and green | Orange and red | *Orange and blue
exam: «Circle the word that is NOT a noun» asks the opposite of «Circle the noun». Which instruction is the opposite of «Circle the word that is NOT a noun»? | Underline every noun | Circle the word that is not a verb | Circle the word that is a verb | *Circle the word that is a noun
